# Improved AMP: a trig whose condition fails is not faded for. The BD track holds trigs on steps 1, 2 and 3
# (125 ms apart at 120 BPM), HLD 57 holds each hit into the next and ENV RESET is at AMP. Each take plays
# the pattern three times (trigs from 0, 2000 and 4000 ms; the sound ends in between: 3 hits).
# No condition: 6 dips (before steps 2 and 3 of each time). Step 2 on FILL, FILL mode off: it never plays,
# 3 dips, and the voice is not silenced before step 2 (that would end the hit: 6 hits). Step 2 on 2:2: it
# plays the second time only, 4 dips.
# The condition: in GRID RECORDING on the TRIG page, hold the trig and turn D (PRB, TRC while a trig is
# held). The list runs 1 % to 100 %, FILL, !FILL, PRE, !PRE, NEI, !NEI, 1ST, !1ST, 1:2, 2:2 ... 8:8. With
# the trig held, `nudge D +1 per 6` shows the unlocked value, a second one locks 100 %, and from there a
# nudge of N steps of 6 counts moves N places (seen on rytm-emu, 10 Nov 2026: FILL after
# +1, 2:2 after +10; a re-hold shows 100 % whatever is locked, so the value is compared before release).
# Taking the trig off and placing it again clears its condition. FILL mode has to be off (the case does
# not set it): with FILL latched, `cfill` has 6 dips.
# Expected from the module's README and code and from stock's manual; not yet run on the unit.
# The BD track needs a sound that rings with the AMP envelope open.
# Changes the tempo, the BD track's AMP page and its ENV RESET in the active kit, and the BD track of the
# active pattern, which it clears; ends at 120 BPM, ENV RESET OFF, HLD 0, the track empty.
name: improved-amp-prefade-cond
state: changes
transport: any
target: unit

hold TRK
key BD
release TRK
# Tempo to 120.0: down to the bottom (30.0), then 90 BPM up, a step of the tempo screen's LEVEL being 1 BPM.
key TEMPO
enc LEVEL -127 x64
nudge LEVEL +21 per 6 x4
nudge LEVEL +6 per 6
wait 500
screen tempo
expect tempo == ref region 40 15 88 33
key NO
key AMP
cc 78 0
cc 79 57
cc 80 55
cc 81 0
cc 82 0
cc 83 0
cc 10 64
cc 7 100
hold FUNC
wait 300
key MUTE
release FUNC
key UP x4
key DOWN x4
key YES
key UP x8
key DOWN x2
key LEFT x3
key RIGHT
wait 500
screen er1
expect er1 == ref region 39 26 82 11
key NO x3
key TRIG
key RECORD
wait 300
key T1
key FUNC+PLAY
wait 800
key T1
key T2
key T3
wait 300
key RECORD
wait 300
audio call BD 5400
wait 100
key PLAY
wait 4480
key STOP
wait 900
key RECORD
wait 300
hold T2
wait 400
nudge D +1 per 6 x3
wait 400
screen fill
expect fill == ref region 95 9 33 19
release T2
wait 300
key RECORD
wait 300
audio cfill BD 5400
wait 100
key PLAY
wait 4480
key STOP
wait 900
key RECORD
wait 300
key T2
wait 300
key T2
wait 300
hold T2
wait 400
nudge D +1 per 6 x2
nudge D +10 per 6
wait 400
screen c22
expect c22 == ref region 95 9 33 19
expect c22 != fill region 95 9 33 19
release T2
wait 300
key RECORD
wait 300
audio ctwo BD 5400
wait 100
key PLAY
wait 4480
key STOP
wait 900
hold FUNC
wait 300
key MUTE
release FUNC
key UP x4
key DOWN x4
key YES
key UP x8
key DOWN x2
key LEFT x3
wait 500
screen er0
expect er0 == ref region 39 26 82 11
key NO x3
key RECORD
wait 300
key T1
key FUNC+PLAY
wait 800
key RECORD
cc 79 0

expect call.hits == 3
expect call.dips == 6
expect cfill.hits == 3
expect cfill.dips == 3
expect ctwo.hits == 3
expect ctwo.dips == 4
